{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993644312642001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"balm-feast-mica","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":5},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3a98a5dd46d12d9a24fb81033536193ceb63fa1e369338baff95bf0cc1a137bf","event_uuid":"09d7aaff-c8f4-46ce-94d3-97b58d309e79","position":{"commit_sha":"3f8673e4d71e81338645de582a7eccef34656e9f","position":"1785339392404379001-09d7aaff-c8f4-46ce-94d3-97b58d309e79"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1782753319449326001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bc1abfc2-e0b1-456d-88d4-a9b5f804abb1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c36c-357a-2900-4ed7"},{"link_uuid":"09d7aaff-c8f4-46ce-94d3-97b58d309e79","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5cc0-1005-018e-4085"}],"description":"## Summary\nThe reconciler resolves a ticket's `assignee` to a Jira user on TWO divergent code paths, producing inconsistent results for the same input. An UPDATE strictly resolves the assignee (exact / unique-normalized accountId, else unassign); a CREATE sends the **raw** local string to ACLI/Jira with no resolution, so Jira fuzzy-matches or applies a project-default assignee. Same local value `\"joe\"` therefore yields different outcomes depending on path.\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n1. Local ticket with `assignee=\"joe\"` (not a unique Jira identity — e.g. 3 \"Joe\"s exist).\n2. **CREATE path** (new issue): reconcile creates the Jira issue. **Actual:** Jira assigns it to `joeoakhart@navapbc.com` (fuzzy/default fallback) — a *wrong* user.\n3. **UPDATE path** (already-bound, Jira unassigned): reconcile diffs assignee. **Actual:** `\"joe\"` is unmappable → issue left unassigned (and inbound later clears the local value).\n\n**Expected:** both paths apply the SAME resolution policy: resolve `\"joe\"` → unique accountId if one exists, otherwise leave unassigned — never silently mis-assign to a fuzzy/default user.\n\n## Root Cause\n- **CREATE does NOT validate.** `acli.py:297-298` extracts the raw assignee; `acli_cli_ops.py:241-243` (non-JSON) and `:367-368` (JSON) pass the raw string straight to ACLI. No `validate_assignee_exists` call. ACLI/Jira then fuzzy-resolves or defaults.\n- **UPDATE DOES validate.** `acli.py:347-349` calls `validate_assignee_exists()` before mutating; the diff resolver `outbound_differ.py:506-535` + `outbound_fields.py:372-390` map unmappable → unassign (`\"\"`). Strict matcher: `acli.py:517-606`.\n\n## Proposed Unification\nAdd ONE shared resolver consumed by both paths:\n- New `AcliClient.resolve_assignee_for_mutation(assignee, *, issue_key=None, project_key=None) -> (accountId|None, authoritative: bool)` that wraps `validate_assignee_exists` and classifies the outcome: resolved accountId; `AssigneeNotFoundError` → `(None, authoritative=True)` (definitively unmappable → unassign); transient/API error → `(None, authoritative=False)` (do NOT unassign — preserve, let next pass retry). Preserve the `(acct, authoritative)` tuple rather than collapsing to a bare string, so a transient REST failure never spuriously unassigns.\n- **CREATE** (`create_issue`, no issue key yet) resolves with `project_key=<project>`: resolved accountId → include in payload; unmappable → omit (leave unassigned); transient → omit (avoid mis-assign).\n- **UPDATE** (`update_issue`, has issue key) resolves with `issue_key=<key>` via the same method.\n- The diff-side `_assignee_resolver` collapses to a thin wrapper over the shared method (single source of truth).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CREATE and UPDATE route assignee resolution through ONE shared method; identical input yields identical Jira outcome.\n- [ ] An ambiguous/unmappable assignee (e.g. `\"joe\"`) is left UNASSIGNED on both paths — never fuzzy-matched or defaulted to an unrelated user.\n- [ ] A uniquely-resolvable assignee (exact email/accountId/displayName, or unique normalized variant) is assigned identically on both paths.\n- [ ] Transient resolution failures do NOT unassign (authoritative=False is preserved end-to-end); only authoritative AssigneeNotFoundError unassigns.\n- [ ] CREATE uses project-scope resolution (no issue_key yet); `validate_assignee_exists` already accepts `project_key`.\n- [ ] Tests: CREATE+UPDATE parity for ambiguous, exact, unique-normalized, and transient-error cases.\n\n## Affected Files (initial)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/acli.py` (`create_issue`, `update_issue`, new shared resolver, `validate_assignee_exists`)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/acli_cli_ops.py` (CREATE raw-string call sites)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` / `outbound_fields.py` (diff resolver → wrapper)","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/acli.py","reason":"create_issue/update_issue + shared resolver + validate_assignee_exists"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/acli_cli_ops.py","reason":"CREATE raw-string assignee call sites"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_fields.py","reason":"diff resolver -> thin wrapper"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"_assignee_resolver closure"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","5cc0-1005-018e-4085"],["relates_to","c36c-357a-2900-4ed7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"40cdb33d-f650-4347-9cb1-cfd62ddc4d79","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"544e-0a25-eabb-4220","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Unify assignee resolution across CREATE and UPDATE reconciler paths (CREATE bypasses validate_assignee_exists -> fuzzy/default mis-assignment)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["49f30411-d672-4a81-b90d-3e5b3c7f9f9d","4cb0c902-f55d-42f7-a570-e29c8cda057f","bc1abfc2-e0b1-456d-88d4-a9b5f804abb1","40cdb33d-f650-4347-9cb1-cfd62ddc4d79","0ad5b7f2-da86-451d-a010-c5621a12e79f","09d7aaff-c8f4-46ce-94d3-97b58d309e79"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993644312642001,"uuid":"aea99353-94d6-423a-855f-e5789d023ad9"}